            <div xml:id="d81">

                <pb facs="0239" n="154" sameAs="frus:frus1919v02/pg154"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">839.51/2031</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Minister in the
                        Dominican Republic</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Russell</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1919-06-14"><hi rendition="#italic">June 14,
                        1919</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 294</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: The Department has had under consideration
                    the request made by the Military Governor of the Dominican Republic to transfer
                    to the Military Government the collection of the internal revenues of the
                    Republic.</p>
                <pb facs="0240" n="155" xml:id="pg155"/>
                <p>After careful consideration of the subject, the Department has reached the
                    conclusion that it cannot approve the proposed transfer, and you will so inform
                    the Military Governor.</p>
                <p>I am [etc.]</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Frank L. Polk</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
